  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3464 (head e97b5c507), which keeps a repeated tool in `grbl.cps`, `grblhal.cps` and `tinyg.cps`.\n\n1. Issue #3445 asked also for no `M5` and no lift between two sections with the same tool. PR #3464 keeps the `M5`, the lift and the new `S M3` on purpose (its decision file), and its closing line closes #3445. Decide if the dropped part is wanted, and prove that it is safe before a change.\n2. No test asserts `S M3` before the first feed of a section that keeps its tool, and none uses a different spindle speed with the same tool. The scripts write it. Add the two pins.\n3. No test covers the same-tool rule for each post with a manual tool change. Only `tormach_same_tool.rs` and `grbl_family_same_tool.rs` exist. Add a table over these posts.\n4. `mach3.cps` (PR #2515, not merged) must take the same rule before it merges, or with a follow-up.\n5. `assets/posts/carvera.cps:393` writes `M6 Tn` for each section. Check if it needs the rule (the Carvera has an automatic changer: a repeated `M6` of the same tool can be without effect or can start a tool measure).\n",
